<title>FRANCE: UAP, Axa fall on U.S. selling.</title>
<headline>UAP, Axa fall on U.S. selling.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in merger partners Union des Assurances de Paris (UAP) and Axa fell on the Paris bourse on Monday on profit-taking, notably by U.S. funds, traders said.</p>
<p>They said the selling was probably spurred by U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission rules which do not recognise the &quot;certificates of guaranteed value&quot; offered by Axa as part of the complex share swap agreement announced last week. It entails an exchange of four Axa shares plus four certificates -- guaranteeing a minimum price -- for 10 UAP shares.</p>
<p>Axa shares were down 2.25 percent at 294.80 francs at 1300 GMT, while UAP shares were down 1.72 percent at 131.80 francs.</p>
<p>Market sources said the SEC rules led U.S. funds to sell their UAP shares.</p>
